 "method": [
  "Open-loop Poisson arrivals at a fixed rate; the rate grows until a probe misses the target, then bisects, then the best rate is confirmed over full windows. TTFT counts from the request's send (queueing included); TPOT per request is (last token - first token) / (output tokens - 1); a failed request is an infinite latency. Requests keep arriving until the last measured one finishes, so the load stays steady for all of them. Board power is nvidia-smi's every second, averaged over each window.",
  "Stability: nvidia-smi every second over the whole measurement (power, SM clock, temperature, utilisation, clock-event reasons and, from econ 0.0.6, the PCIe link), with each GPU's state at the start and the end; under load means at 50 % utilisation or above.",
  "MBU (an estimate): engine steps per second times the bytes of weights a step reads, over the GPUs' datasheet bandwidth; the KV cache's reads are not counted."
 ]
